(a) It shall be unlawful to attach or erect a balcony or other structures to a building so as to extend over any portion of a public sidewalk, except upon the authorization of the Director of Business Development Services and upon compliance with all applicable sections of this Code or other ordinances of Macon-Bibb County, including this section.
(b) Balconies and awnings shall be designed by an architect or an engineer licensed to practice in the state and the plans and specifications for balconies presented to Macon-Bibb County for approval shall bear the official registration seal of the architect or engineer. The plans and specifications shall be submitted to and approved by the planning and zoning commission before the Director of Business Development Services authorizes the balconies or awnings.
(c) The granting of permission to construct these balconies or awnings so as to extend over the public sidewalks shall be contingent upon the owner, lessor or lessee of the building onto which the balconies are constructed, the owner of the land upon which the building is erected and all creditors secured by all or a part of the land or building entering into an agreement with Macon-Bibb County which shall include but not be limited to agreements by the owner or lessee of the building to which the balconies or awnings are attached to:
(1) Construct and maintain the balconies so as to prevent any portion thereof from becoming detached and falling to the street or sidewalk below;
(2) Remove any or all of the balconies without cost to the county within a 90-day period after the Commission directs such removal by mailing a notice to remove the balconies to the owner, or lessee at an address set forth in the agreement;
(3) When in the opinion of the Director of Business Development Services it is deemed appropriate, furnish and maintain a bond, at no expense to Macon-Bibb County, with a satisfactory corporate surety, to guarantee the performance of the principal in removing the balconies as provided for in subsection (c)(2) of this section;
(4) Indemnify and hold the county, its officers, agents and employees harmless from any and all claims arising out of the construction, maintenance, use of or removal of any and all of the balconies, including claims arising out of persons falling or jumping from the balconies or arising out of objects being dropped or thrown from the balconies;
(5) Furnish a policy of public liability insurance and property damage insurance satisfactory to Macon-Bibb County naming it as a named insured or an additional named insured, in an amount approved by the county's risk manager, which protects Macon-Bibb County and its officers, agents and employees from claims arising out of the construction, maintenance, use of or removal of the balconies, including claims arising out of any person falling or jumping from any such balcony or throwing or dropping any object from a balcony;
(6) Provide insurance covering the agreement to indemnify and hold Macon-Bibb County and its officers, agents and employees harmless from any and all claims arising out of construction, maintenance, use of or removal of any or all of the balconies, including claims arising out of persons falling or jumping from the balconies or similar structures or arising out of objects being thrown or dropped from the balconies, with a further agreement that the obligation to indemnify and hold the county and its officers, agents and employees harmless shall not be limited to the amount of the public liability and property damage insurance naming the county as a named insured or an additional named insured; and
(d) Each request for permission to erect those balconies or awnings shall be accompanied by a title certificate of an attorney authorized to practice law in the state setting forth the names and the addresses of the owner and lessee of the building and the land on which it is erected, the names and addresses of any creditors who are secured by all or any part of the land or building involved, together with sufficient information as to the terms of any leases on the land or building, the corporate names of any of the parties sufficient to accurately disclose the names of any of the parties required in the agreement between Macon-Bibb County and the parties desiring to construct the balconies or awnings, which agreement shall be executed by all the parties desiring to construct the balconies or awnings, which agreement shall be executed by all the parties prior to the issuance of any building permit for the construction of the balconies or similar structures. The agreement shall be binding on all the parties, their heirs, administrators, assigns and successors in title, and upon the execution of the agreement it shall be filed in the Office of the Clerk of the Superior Court of Bibb County.
(Ord. No. O-15-0030, § 1, 7-21-2015)

2459:
(a) For purposes of this Section, the term "Certificate of Good Standing" shall refer to a certification prepared by an individual, either in his or her own name, or on behalf of an entity which the individual owns or over which the individual exercises managerial control. The Macon-Bibb County Government may prepare the form of the certification and amend it from time to time. The Certificate of Good Standing shall include the following information:
(1) The name of the applicant;
(2) The name of the subject of the Certificate, if different from the applicant;
(3) The benefit or privilege for which the applicant is applying;
(4) (A) If the subject is an individual, then a listing of all business entities in which the individual has a direct or indirect ownership interest of 25% or more, or over which the individual exercises legal control;
(B) If the subject is an entity, then a listing of all individuals who have a direct or indirect ownership interest of 25% of more in the subject entity, or who exercise legal control of the entity;
(5) A sworn statement that the information contained in the Certificate is true and complete to the best of the individual's available knowledge;
(6) A sworn statement that none of the individuals or entities listed therein are more than 90 days delinquent on the payment of ad valorem property taxes; and
(7) Any other information or statements deemed necessary by the Macon-Bibb County Government.
(b) No person or entity shall be eligible for any of the following privileges unless they provide one or more Certificates of Good Standing in accordance with this Section to the official or department responsible for managing the privilege in question:
(1) Obtaining or renewing any building permit, plat approval, building inspection report, certificate of occupancy, alcohol license, or privilege license;
(2) Being appointed to any board or position of trust requiring the confirmation of the Macon-Bibb County Commission;
(3) Being awarded any contract pursuant to a formal competitive sealed bid process under Sec. 19-5.1 of this Code or pursuant to a formal competitive sealed proposals process under Sec. 19-5.2 of this Code;
(4) Being awarded any contract with an estimated or actual cost in excess of $50,000 within a single fiscal year, except for contracts awarded on an emergency basis;
(5) Purchasing any surplus real property from the Macon-Bibb County Government; or
(6) Bidding on any real property that is being auctioned by the Tax Commissioner of Macon-Bibb County.
(c) Before any individual shall be granted any of the privileges described in subsection (b) of this Section, such individual shall provide:
(1) A Certificate of Good Standing in such individual's own name; and
(2) If the individual is applying for any privilege under subsection (b)(1) of this Section, then a Certificate of Good Standing for the owner of the real property where construction or regulated business activities are occurring.
(d) Before any legal entity shall be granted any of the privileges described in subsection (b) of this Section, such entity shall provide:
(1) A Certificate of Good Standing in such entity's name;
(2) A Certificate of Good Standing completed by each individual owner identified in the entity's Certificate of Good Standing; and
(3) If the entity is applying for any privilege under subsection (b)(1) of this Section, then a Certificate of Good Standing for the owner of the real property where construction or regulated business activities are occurring.
(e) (1) Any privilege that is subject to the requirements of this Section may be denied in the event that false, incomplete, or inaccurate information is provided on any Certificate of Good Standing form submitted.
(2) Any privilege that is subject to the requirements of this Section may be revoked, terminated, or invalidated upon notice and an opportunity for a hearing as to any subsequent finding that, at the time any Certificate of Good Standing was submitted in connection with such privilege, it contained false, incomplete, or inaccurate information. For privileges listed under subsection (b)(1) of this Section, this may include, without limitation, the termination or revocation of any permit, license, approval or authorization previously granted. For privileges listed under subsection (b)(2) of this Section, this may include, without limitation, removal or termination from the appointed position. For privileges listed under subsections (b)(3) or (b)(4) of this Section, this may include, without limitation, and notwithstanding any contractual terms to the contrary, immediate termination of the contract for cause, re-awarding of any contract to a different vendor in accordance with applicable procurement laws, or debarring the applicant from participating in future procurement matters of Macon-Bibb County. For privileges listed under subsections (b)(5) or (b)(6) of this Section, this may include invalidating any sales contract or bid, awarding the sale to the next-highest bidder, or action by Macon-Bibb County to reverse a completed sale.
(3) In the event that false, incomplete, or inaccurate information is provided on any Certificate of Good Standing, the denial or revocation actions taken by Macon-Bibb County shall not be limited to the specific privileges being applied for at the time of the false, incomplete, or inaccurate statement, but may include any or all other privileges granted by Macon-Bibb County to the subject of such Certificate, to the greatest extent of the law.
(4) The remedies in this subsection are cumulative and in addition to any other civil or criminal penalties that may be applied under the law to any person or entity for making false, incomplete, or inaccurate statements on any Certificate of Good Standing.
(5) The use of any artifice or scheme for the purpose of, or which has the effect of, avoiding the reporting requirements of this Section shall be grounds for the denial or revocation of any privilege in accordance with this subsection (e) as though the Certificate of Good Standing knowingly contained false, incomplete, or inaccurate information.
(f) The mayor and his or her designee shall have the authority to waive any requirement imposed under this Section upon making a written determination that enforcing the requirement would work an undue hardship on the applicant or on Macon-Bibb County.
(g) The mayor and his or her designee shall have the authority to impose compliance with this Section as an additional requirement on any person or entity which is seeking or receiving any privilege, favor, or honor from the Macon-Bibb County Government as a condition thereof.
(h) Compliance with this Section shall not, by itself, be sufficient to entitle any applicant to any grant of privilege from Macon-Bibb County. Applicants must also comply with all other applicable requirements for any desired privilege. In the event that any person or entity pays any lawfully levied and due ad valorem taxes for the purpose of applying for, obtaining, or supporting any application for any privilege that is subject to the requirements of this section, such taxes shall not be refunded notwithstanding the applicant's success or failure in obtaining the desired privilege.
